      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I really like the ability of instance creators to be able to disable content in instances. Most worlds don't have any content disabled. Running a group public Black Cat and don't want people to sticker awful shit on the walls or scatter prints of TOS breaking images around the world? You can now disable them. Great! \n\nBut allowing instance creators to override content disabled by a world creator is a baffling decision to me. World creators should have the final say of what's allowed IN THEIR WORLDS. If a world creator disables stickers because they don't work and an instance creator makes an instance and enables them anyway then what's the point of the world creator having that choice to begin with? This only effects a minority of worlds but it's such a strange decision that can ruin a world creator's vision or artistic design.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
