      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm fully against this, let people do what they want in their own instances, they can break all the rules anyways with custom avatars. You can make flying avatars, you can place sticker-like content with custom avatars, you can easily make own emojis with custom avatar.\n\nSo stop trying to prey into what people do in their own private space.\n\nIts my own instance where im with friends so any issues of privacy or cheating dont apply, as there is no one here to cheat against when we all wanted to experience the world in this way.\n\nEspecially that creators often disallow stuff for no reason, some things can't even be re-enabled, like portals, making you stuck in basically broken world and needing to ask everyone to join on you manually when exploring with a group...",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
