  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "To preface this, I'm 50/50 on this one. I understand *why* the system is set up like this, it just seems strange to me that the current implementation of \"instance settings\" allows people to disrespect a world creator's wishes if the instance isn't public.\n\nIf a world creator doesn't want people to stickerbomb their world or litter it with prints, then I can see why people would argue that that choice should always be respected.\n\nThis is especially worrisome when drones are currently able to influence rigidbodies: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1601-drones-should-not-influence-pickups-rigidbodies-in-worlds",
